#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The quantum-HPC integration challenge {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-"
"challenge}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"High-performance computing (HPC) workflows often require seamless "
"coordination between classical compute clusters and quantum processing units"
" (QPUs). Different quantum hardware backends and services expose distinct "
"authentication mechanisms, wire formats, and job lifecycle APIs. Integrating"
" IBM Quantum systems into HPC workload managers (such as Slurm) requires a "
"clean, standard interface for resource acquisition, job execution, and "
"session management.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What QRMI is {#what-qrmi-is}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** is a middleware library"
" written in Rust that standardizes access to quantum hardware from HPC "
"schedulers and classical applications. It exposes a single unified lifecycle"
" API:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QRMI is published as an open-source project at [github.com/qiskit-"
"community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) and is described "
"in the overview paper "
"[arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key design choices {#key-design-choices}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Resource lifecycle, not circuit compilation.** QRMI handles the "
"acquire/submit/poll/release lifecycle and nothing else. Circuit compilation,"
" optimization, and transpilation remain in the application layer (for "
"example, Qiskit). This keeps the interface minimal and composable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Vendor portability model.** While QRMI provides common job-management "
"calls (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) "
"across supported hardware backends, changing vendors also requires different"
" compilation passes, vendor-specific payload construction, and result "
"decoding in the application layer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Native IBM payload format.** For IBM Quantum backends, QRMI uses OpenQASM "
"3 JSON payloads (`QiskitPrimitive`) conforming to the Qiskit Runtime "
"schema.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration through environment variables.** Credentials and endpoint "
"URLs are read from environment variables at runtime. In an HPC cluster, the "
"Slurm QRMI SPANK plugin sets these automatically when a job is dispatched. "
"In a notebook or interactive session, you load them from a `.env` file. "
"Application code never contains hardcoded credentials or endpoint URLs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**HPC scheduler integration through GRES.** When a Slurm job requests "
"quantum resources using the QRMI SPANK plugin interface (`#SBATCH "
"--gres=qpu:1` and `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), the plugin injects "
"`QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` and `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` into the job environment. "
"Applications call `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` to discover which "
"resources were allocated &mdash; no hardcoded backend names required. "
"`QRMIService` wraps this pattern for Qiskit users.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The core API calls {#the-core-api-calls}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call | Purpose |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Acquire access to the resource (for example, opens a dedicated session); returns a lock token |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Retrieve backend capabilities (qubits, gates, coupling map) as JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Submit a quantum job; returns a job ID |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | Poll job status (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Retrieve completed job results as a raw JSON string |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Cancel or clean up a job |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | Release the resource lock (for example, closes the session) |\n"
msgstr ""

