#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map the classical problem to a quantum resource {#step-1-map-the-"
"classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first step in any QRMI workflow is to create a `QuantumResource` object "
"and verify that it is accessible.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`get_target()` retrieves the backend's hardware description (qubit count, "
"basis gates, coupling map) and packages it as a Qiskit `Target` object, "
"which the transpiler uses in Step 2.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution "
"{#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before submission, use Qiskit to transpile the circuit to the backend's "
"instruction set architecture (ISA), using the `Target` object retrieved in "
"Step 1.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The example then builds a `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, which wraps the "
"OpenQASM 3 circuit string and job metadata into the IBM primitive schema.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using QRMI primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the payload built, the example submits the job and polls for "
"completion. `task_start()` returns a job ID immediately; `task_status()` is "
"polled until the status is no longer `Queued`/`Running`. Results are "
"retrieved as a raw JSON string and parsed to extract measurement samples.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following cell keeps acquisition, execution, and cleanup together so "
"that failures after acquisition still release a notebook-owned session.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Higher-level Qiskit interface: QRMIService and SamplerV2 {#higher-level-"
"qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The raw lifecycle above provides explicit control over every call. For "
"standard Qiskit workflows, QRMI provides a `SamplerV2` primitive "
"implementing `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Lifecycle management\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`SamplerV2` handles payload serialization, submission (`task_start`), "
"polling, and result decoding. In an HPC batch setting (for example, with "
"Slurm), allocation and release are managed by the scheduler and the SPANK "
"plugin. In an interactive Python session using direct low-level API objects,"
" `acquire()` and `release()` can be used to explicitly manage dedicated "
"sessions.\n"
msgstr ""

